# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copyrighted game data — NEVER commit.
# Serious Sam: Next Encounter is (c) Climax / Take-Two / Croteam; the disc
# image, its extracted files, and anything converted from them stay local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The disc and its extracted contents (keep only the "how to populate" note).
orig/*
!orig/README.md

# Everything the tools/ extract or convert from orig/: meshes, textures,
# models, sounds, text, worlds, renders. All derived from the game's assets.
build/

# Developer material from NE's production (SE1 1.04 tools, GC entity DLLs,
# source worlds and models). Proprietary; reference only, never commit.
dev/

# Ghidra project: the database embeds main.dol's bytes and disassembly.
ghidra/*.gpr
ghidra/*.rep/
ghidra/*.lock
ghidra/*.lock~

# Belt and braces: disc images, executables and asset formats anywhere in
# the tree. pc/engine and ref/ are submodules, so these never match there.
*.rvz
*.iso
*.gcm
*.gcz
*.ciso
*.wbfs
*.nkit.*
*.dol
*.elf
*.ssg
*.ssw
*.sst
*.tdb
*.spt
*.spd
*.bnr
*.bik
*.Gui
StreamData.dat
# SE1 retail archives (needed to run stock SE1; not ours to ship).
*.gro

# Converted / generated media. Whatever tools/ or SE1's converters make from
# the game's assets is still the game's: models, textures, skeletons and
# animations, audio, fonts, renders. SE1 worlds (*.wld) are deliberately NOT
# listed here.
*.mdl
*.tex
*.tga
*.bmp
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.dds
*.obj
*.mtl
*.ska
*.bm
*.an
*.smc
*.fnt
*.wav
*.ogg
*.mp3
*.aif
*.aiff
*.dsp
*.adp
# Maya / Climax model sources from dev/
*.clm
*.ma
*.mb

